+// fitLiSPSM fits a Light Space Perspective Shadow Map and reports whether it managed to
+// (false means the configuration is degenerate and the caller should fall back).
+//
+// The construction is three matrices composed into the world→light-clip matrix the
+// depth pass and the lit shaders share:
+//
+//	L  world → light space: a basis with the light direction as z and, as y, the view
+//	   direction with the light direction projected out — so the warp axis lies in the
+//	   plane the perspective error actually lives in. Translated so the warp's apex
+//	   sits at y=0.
+//	P  the warp itself: w = y, so everything divides by distance along the warp axis.
+//	   Points near the viewer (small y) spread out, taking more of the map; distant
+//	   ones compress. y maps to [-1,1] through the standard 1D perspective mapping.
+//	N  a final affine normalize of x and z into the clip cube, from the warped bounds
+//	   actually measured — cheaper to get right than deriving the coefficients, and it
+//	   handles a lopsided body without special cases.
+//
