+
+	// Light space is anchored at the EYE, not the world origin, exactly as the paper's
+	// implementation places its light view (look from eyePos along the light). The warp
+	// divides by the distance along the warp axis, so it wants coordinates measured in
+	// tens, not in whatever absolute numbers the world happens to use: anchored at the
+	// origin, a scene a few hundred units out already loses enough float precision in
+	// that divide to break the depth comparison outright. Relative to the eye, the
+	// numbers stay small wherever the scene sits.
